\\":\\\"fxe61i12\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Terminate high-usage process\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Terminate Next.js dev server (PID 20872) consuming 1240MB memory to relieve system pressure\\\",\\\"commandPreview\\\":\\\"taskkill /F /PID 20872\\\",\\\"commandId\\\":\\\"kill_process\\\",\\\"commandArgs\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Terminate Next.js dev server (PID 20872) consuming 1240MB memory to relieve system pressure\\\",\\\"pids\\\":[20872],\\\"summary\\\":\\\"System Memory 92.9%, Disk 88.6%. High memory is driven by a Next.js dev server (1.2GB) and external Chrome tabs. Recommended to restart the dev server, close browser tabs, and free up system disk space.\\\",\\\"target_process\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"allowed_pids\\\":[3124,4716,4800,5912,6016,6052,6664,7620,8464,9044,9400,9728,9844,9992,10244,10920,11368,12720,13392,15428,15684,16208,18508,20584,20872,21348,21500,22356,22840,23452,23612,25472,25484],\\\"protected_pids\\\":[3156,6504],\\\"issue_source\\\":\\\"external\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"dps6825a\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Open system storage management\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Open Windows Storage Settings to free up disk space (System disk 88.6% full)\\\",\\\"commandPreview\\\":\\\"Open operating system storage settings\\\",\\\"commandId\\\":\\\"open_system_storage_manager\\\",\\\"commandArgs\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Open Windows Storage Settings to free up disk space (System disk 88.6% full)\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"System Memory 92.9%, Disk 88.6%. High memory is driven by a Next.js dev server (1.2GB) and external Chrome tabs. Recommended to restart the dev server, close browser tabs, and free up system disk space.\\\",\\\"target_process\\\":\\\"System\\\"}}]},\\\"snapshot\\\":{\\\"triggeredTypes\\\":[\\\"memory\\\"],\\\"cpuUsage\\\":0.22968444309157451,\\\"memoryUsage\\\":0.9226017848626832,\\\"totalMemoryMb\\\":16226,\\\"diskUsage\\\":0.886743499233418},\\\"stream\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"statusText\\\":\\\"Diagnosis completed\\\",\\\"thinkingText\\\":\\\"**Analyzing System Load**\\\\n\\\\nMy current focus is on understanding the system's performance. I'm observing that while CPU usage is within normal parameters, memory utilization is quite high. This discrepancy is a key area for further investigation.\\\\n\\\\n**Investigating Disk Space**\\\\n\\\\nI'm now noticing the system disk is nearly full, at 88.67%. Simultaneously, I'm calculating Trae's total memory consumption across various processes, which is proving to be a significant portion of the system's ~16 GB RAM.\\\\n\\\\n**Calculating Memory Usage**\\\\n\\\\nMy current analysis reveals that Trae's total memory consumption is approximately 4.5 GB out of the system's 16 GB. This figure includes various Node.js processes, specifically those related to Next.js development, which were spawned under Trae.\\\\n\\\\n**Monitoring Process Memory**\\\\n\\\\nI've detailed the memory breakdown of key processes. The Next.js server consumes a substantial 1240 MB, while multiple Chrome instances collectively use around 2255 MB. This recurring high memory usage, especially from user applications, is a persistent concern.\\\\n\\\\n**Evaluating Memory Contributors**\\\\n\\\\nI am now assessing memory usage more granularly. While Trae’s Next.js server is a significant factor, the combined usage from numerous Chrome tabs and third-party extensions like the ChatGPT one is also substantial. I will suggest closing unnecessary browser tabs.\\\\n\\\\n**Clearing System Storage**\\\\n\\\\nI'm now focused on freeing up disk space by opening the system storage manager. My ongoing analysis confirms high memory usage, primarily driven by Chrome tabs and the Next.js development server, which is a consistent pattern in recent sessions.\\\\n\\\\n**Addressing Memory Spikes**\\\\n\\\\nI'm now looking into actionable steps. I will offer to terminate the Next.js development server, which is a significant memory hog. I'm also preparing to open the system storage manager to address the high disk usage, though it's not yet critical.\\\\n\\\\n**Terminating Next.js Process**\\\\n\\\\nI am now preparing to execute a command to terminate the Next.js development server, identified by PID 20872. This action is intended to alleviate significant memory consumption by this specific Node.js process, contributing to overall system performance improvements.\\\\n\\\\n**Reducing Memory Load**\\\\n\\\\nI am actively working to reduce the system's memory footprint. My immediate action will be to terminate the Next.js development server process (PID 20872) which is currently consuming a significant amount of RAM, contributing to overall system strain.\\\\n\\\\n**Closing Browser Tabs**\\\\n\\\\nI am now focusing on reducing memory usage by addressing the numerous Chrome tabs and the third-party ChatGPT extension. These, combined with the Next.js server, are the primary culprits behind the elevated RAM consumption.\\\\n\\\\n**Refining Process Targets**\\\\n\\\\nI am now carefully considering the specific processes to terminate. While initially targeting PID 20872 for the Next.js server, I've realized it's part of a process tree. I will proceed by terminating PID 20872 to address the immediate memory drain.\\\\n\\\\n**Analyzing Extension Impact**\\\\n\\\\nI've refined my understanding of memory contributors. While the Next.js server and Chrome tabs remain primary concerns, I've noted the AI extension uses nearly 500MB. I will note this in the details, but prioritize the Next.js server for termination.\\\\n\\\\n**Executing Process Termination**\\\\n\\\\nI'm now executing the command to terminate PID 20872, the Next.js development server. This targeted action aims to directly reduce the significant memory load, specifically the 1.2GB consumed by this Node.js process, as identified in my analysis.\\\\n\\\\n**Reducing Memory Pressure**\\\\n\\\\nI am now working to alleviate the system's memory pressure. My primary action is terminating the Next.js development server, wh