d will provide options for managing `codex.exe`.\\\\n\\\\n**Managing Extension Usage**\\\\n\\\\nI've identified `codex.exe`, the language server for an AI extension, consuming a significant 548MB. I'm considering offering the `manage_extension` tool, although this amount might be typical for local AI servers. I'll present this as an option.\\\\n\\\\n**Evaluating Process Candidates**\\\\n\\\\nI'm currently evaluating several processes for potential intervention. The Next.js development server, Chrome renderer processes, and `codex.exe` are all significant memory consumers, but I'm prioritizing the Next.js server for immediate action due to its recurring history and recoverability.\\\\n\\\\n**Disabling Redundant Extensions**\\\\n\\\\nI'm now looking at how to manage extensions. I've identified that `codex.exe` might be tied to an AI extension, and I'm considering disabling it as a potential solution to free up resources.\\\\n\\\\n**Refining Termination Strategy**\\\\n\\\\nI'm refining my approach to process termination. While I can directly address Trae processes, I need to ensure that for non-Trae processes like Node, the correct executable name is used, and that I suggest manual execution rather than automatic.\\\\n\\\\n**Finalizing Termination Plan**\\\\n\\\\nI'm preparing to issue specific commands. I will terminate the Next.js development server by PID and will disable the associated AI extension if deemed appropriate, ensuring clear descriptions and summaries for each action.\\\\n\\\\n**Updating Extension Management**\\\\n\\\\nI've refined the description for the `manage_extension` call to include CPU percentage for the `codex.exe` child process, ensuring it aligns with best practices for providing comprehensive diagnostic details.\\\\n\\\\n**Implementing Termination Sequence**\\\\n\\\\nI am now ready to execute the planned termination sequence, focusing on the identified Next.js development server and providing an option to manage the `codex.exe` process via extension management.\\\\n\\\\n**Managing Extension Options**\\\\n\\\\nI am now presenting the user with actionable choices regarding the `codex.exe` process, offering to disable the `openai.chatgpt` extension to reclaim approximately 548MB of memory, considering its historical context and recoverability.\\\",\\\"thinkingCollapsed\\\":true,\\\"answerText\\\":\\\"System Memory 90.6%. Next.js dev server and Chrome tabs are consuming significant memory. Recommended to restart the dev server and close heavy browser tabs.\\\",\\\"traceid\\\":\\\"ece55a8f6a27288f1e73eb0e9a6989d3\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":1786372484679}},{\\\"diagnosis\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"f8185b07-f92a-4fef-929b-c0ce9037bfb6\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1786279718463,\\\"summary\\\":\\\"System Disk 98.4%, Memory 87.4%. System drive critically full. Recommended to free up space via storage manager and optionally terminate Next.js dev server (PID 19704) consuming 2GB memory.\\\",\\\"cause\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"recommendation\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"triggeredTypes\\\":[\\\"disk\\\"],\\\"actions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"0uv34hjv\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Open system storage management\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Open Windows Storage settings to free up disk space. System disk has only 2GB free.\\\",\\\"commandPreview\\\":\\\"Open operating system storage settings\\\",\\\"commandId\\\":\\\"open_system_storage_manager\\\",\\\"commandArgs\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Open Windows Storage settings to free up disk space. System disk has only 2GB free.\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"System Disk 98.4%, Memory 87.4%. System drive critically full. Recommended to free up space via storage manager and optionally terminate Next.js dev server (PID 19704) consuming 2GB memory.\\\",\\\"target_process\\\":\\\"System\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"4he72ryi\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Terminate high-usage process\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Terminate Next.js dev server (PID 19704) consuming 2,038 MB memory.\\\",\\\"commandPreview\\\":\\\"taskkill /F /PID 19704\\\",\\\"commandId\\\"