\\",\\\"commandArgs\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Open Windows storage settings to clean up system disk space.\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"System Disk 97.9%, Memory 79.2%. System disk has only ~2.4 GB free space. Recurring pattern of high disk usage and Next.js dev server consuming 1.3GB memory. Recommended to open system storage manager to free up space and terminate the dev server.\\\",\\\"target_process\\\":\\\"System\\\"}},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"mvd7b1te\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Terminate high-usage process\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Terminate Next.js dev server (PID 19704, 1.3GB memory) to free up system memory.\\\",\\\"commandPreview\\\":\\\"taskkill /F /PID 19704 /PID 19740\\\",\\\"commandId\\\":\\\"kill_process\\\",\\\"commandArgs\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Terminate Next.js dev server (PID 19704, 1.3GB memory) to free up system memory.\\\",\\\"pids\\\":[19704,19740],\\\"summary\\\":\\\"System Disk 97.9%, Memory 79.2%. System disk has only ~2.4 GB free space. Recurring pattern of high disk usage and Next.js dev server consuming 1.3GB memory. Recommended to open system storage manager to free up space and terminate the dev server.\\\",\\\"target_process\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"allowed_pids\\\":[1844,5236,7232,7304,8748,9808,10744,11080,11832,13884,13992,14228,15000,15008,15436,16296,16588,17600,18272,18284,18548,18608,19392,19704,19740,19888,20216,21464,21608,22064,22320,23852],\\\"protected_pids\\\":[24800,14712],\\\"issue_source\\\":\\\"external\\\"}}]},\\\"snapshot\\\":{\\\"triggeredTypes\\\":[\\\"disk\\\"],\\\"cpuUsage\\\":0.1836045137320447,\\\"memoryUsage\\\":0.7898967075299481,\\\"totalMemoryMb\\\":16226,\\\"diskUsage\\\":0.9797194911593364},\\\"stream\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"statusText\\\":\\\"Diagnosis completed\\\",\\\"thinkingText\\\":\\\"**Analyzing System Bottlenecks**\\\\n\\\\nMy current focus is on interpreting the provided system resource metrics. I see the CPU is relatively idle, but memory is quite high at nearly 80%. The disk usage is critically high at 97.9%, indicating a potential bottleneck there.\\\\n\\\\n**Investigating Disk Pressure**\\\\n\\\\nThe system disk is showing extreme pressure, though most of it appears to stem from external factors. I'm now diving into the memory consumption specifically within Trae's processes.\\\\n\\\\n**Analyzing Trae Processes**\\\\n\\\\nI'm now examining the memory distribution across Trae's processes. A significant portion appears to be consumed by the Next.js dev server, which is utilizing over 1.3 GB. The total memory footprint for all Trae-related processes is approximately 3.9 GB.\\\\n\\\\n**Diagnosing Disk Space**\\\\n\\\\nMy analysis confirms the system disk is critically full at 97.9%. While Trae's own files are within limits, external factors are clearly the cause. I'm now scrutinizing other processes, like Chrome, to identify where this space is being consumed.\\\\n\\\\n**Identifying Disk Saturation**\\\\n\\\\nI've confirmed the system disk is critically full, with only 2.4 GB remaining. Trae's direct usage is minimal, so the pressure is from external sources. I also noted the Next.js dev server continues to consume substantial memory.\\\\n\\\\n**Clearing Disk and Memory**\\\\n\\\\nI've identified the Next.js dev server as a persistent high-memory consumer and the system disk as critically full due to external factors. I'll proceed with cleaning the disk and consider terminating the Next.js server if memory needs immediate freeing.\\\\n\\\\n**Addressing Disk and Memory**\\\\n\\\\nI've confirmed the system disk is critically full due to external factors, while the Next.js dev server remains a significant memory hog. I will now open the storage manager and terminate the dev server process to alleviate both issues.\\\\n\\\\n**Clearing Disk and Memory**\\\\n\\\\nI've confirmed the system disk is critically full at 97.9% with only 2.4 GB free, and the Next.js dev server is consuming 1.3 GB of memory. External factors are causing the disk pressure. I will now open the storage manager and terminate the dev server process.\\\\n\\\\n**Clearing System Resources**\\\\n\\\\nI've identified the Next.js dev server as a consistent memory drain and the system disk is critically full due to external factors. I'm now opening the storage manager to clear space and will terminate the dev server to alleviate immediate pressure.\\\\n\\\\n**Targeting Processes for Cleanup**\\\\n\\\\nI've confirmed the Next.js dev server is PID 19704, consuming significant memory. I will target both this PID and its parent, 19740, for termination to ensure a complete cleanup.\\\\n\\\\n**Refining Cleanup Targets**\\\\n\\\\nI've identified the Next.js dev server (PID 19704) as the process to target for memory cleanup. For system disk issues, the schema suggests \\\\\\\"System\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\"Windows\\\\\\\". I will use \\\\\\\"Windows Explorer\\\\\\\" for the storage manager to precisely address the disk space issue.\\\\n\\\\n**Executing Cleanup Actions**\\\\n\\\\nI am now initiating the process to open the system storage manager and terminate the identified Next.js dev server processes to address both critical disk space and high memory utilization.\\\",\\\"thinkingCollapsed\\\":true,\\\"answerText\\\":\\\"System Disk 97.9%, Memory 79.2%. System disk has only ≈2.4 GB free space. Recurring pattern of high disk usage and Next.js dev server consuming 1.3GB memory. Recommended to open system storage manager to free up space and terminate the dev server.\\\",\\\"traceid\\\":\\\"fd5ff999c049b4e5a5d96b0c5e0240f5\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":1786261626350}}]\",\"workbench.activityBar.location\":\"default\",\"workbench.welcomePage.walkthroughMetadata\":\"[[\\\"Anthropic.claude-code#claude-code-walkthrough\\\",{\\\"firstSeen\\\":1771565686950,\\\"stepIDs\\\":[\\\"welcome\\\",\\\"open-claude\\\",\\\"chat\\\",\\\"sessions\\\"],\\\"manaullyOpened\\\":false}],[\\\"eamodio.gitlens#welcome\\\",{\\\"firstSeen\\\":1771565686950,\\\"stepIDs\\\":[\\\"get-started-community\\\",\